so you're thinking about coming back to  gta online next gen no wait you're  thinking about jumping into gta online  for the first time either way now is a  great time with a more streamlined  experience and lots of handholding for  new players rockstar has made gta online  approachable to anyone  for the first time in a long time gta  online servers are a mixed bag of  experienced players new players and  everyone in between personally i dusted  off my old account from 2014 when dr  dre's the contract dlc dropped  [ __ ] ass  after seven years i was a little  overwhelmed  gta online used to be constant drive-by  attacks remote explosions  bugattis and every millionaire living  right  here  now you can own businesses like clubs  and banks there are dozens of new  vehicles and dlc missions and of course  after all these years the character  customization is mind-boggling if that  seemed a little overwhelming starting  fresh with next gen might just be the  way to go for you let's break down what  starting over looks like  before you create your all new character  you're given loads of fun player options  right out of the gate along with 4  million gta bucks to start  first come selecting a criminal career  you're able to choose your path  cyberpunk style with your options being  executive gun runner nightclub owner or  biker next comes the bunker it's a  little weird but owning a bunker is  required to start it's a safe space for  you your arsenal and your cars there are  a few location options sprinkled around  northern san andreas and they range from  2.2 million dollars to free with this  very last option either way you need to  pick one and choose from a list of  optional upgrades and amenities if  you're getting one of the larger decked  out bunkers i'd suggest getting one of  these stupid little caddies if money  isn't an issue money isn't an issue you  can really take advantage of the space  with all the options they offer yet your  running around speed indoors is pretty  slow  once your bunker is designed how you  like it's time to pick from a selection  of cars and weapons i would advise you  to take your time here as much as i  wanted whatever the [ __ ] this is i  thought about the practicality of  something a little smaller this hvy  night shark has armor options and  surprisingly fast acceleration it's  perfect for getting out of a heist  personally i've seen this thing do  really well in online missions which  we'll discuss a little later anyway you  know what don't don't listen to me pick  what you want and live your life there's  a really nice selection of cars here  same with weapons there are a lot of  solid options here my only suggestion  would be getting something well-rounded  like an assault rifle because you can  always buy more later  money isn't an issue now it's time to  create your fresh-faced character who  has yet to be jaded by life in los  santos i went with the random option  myself and i have zero regrets my dude  looks like a rejected gta 3 character  with a suit and bandana  oh he blinked that's funny  now that you have your very own base and  vehicle and have selected a career path  it's time to leave the bunker and get  your life going your phone will be  blowing up with opportunities pay  attention to these early calls and texts  because you'll get several mission  offers to get you going as well as  information about how to claim great  freebies like a free car from your tuner  buddy howe and even free property  see you ain't even ready for this  also at this point i noticed the game  was running in fidelity mode which  displays at 30 frames per second this  mode isn't bad but if you want those  higher frames i'd suggest performance  mode or performance ray tracing mode to  know more about these three modes check  out our everything to know video in the  description  as far as setting up goes the biggest  stuff is now behind us and now you can  just sit back and start playing some gta  or if you're returning after a long time  it's time to begin your nostalgia trip  once you've made it into town you can  pick up your new cars and check out your  heist apartment that your buddy lester  set up for you from here on out you'll  continue getting mission invites from  familiar faces like martin madrazo  trevor phillips gerald and more if you  accept these early missions you'll find  the perfect blend of fun and nostalgia  without being too tough if you're new or  don't remember these were the same  opening missions offered back in 2013  with the launch of gta online in my  experience these were great to help me  get started all over again in next gen  or if you're a long time active player  these classic missions might be nice to  see in the rotation again and a fun  benefit of starting over all of these  missions are based on your rank as you  level up in your gta online career  you'll be offered more thorough missions  including heists which can earn you  millions  another benefit i've come across is that  like me a lot of people have chosen to  start fresh  mission lobbies are filled with lower  ranked players and we're all just sort  of reliving the early days of gta online  sometimes we screwed up but usually the  whole group would just hit reset and  we'd just try it again or this other  mission where a higher ranked player  just sort of helped me out he wasn't  pushy and he let me drive and do most of  the killing and he was really just there  for support it was pretty great and  after the mission ended he didn't try to  kill me or anything he just took off and  we parted ways  it's kind of weird to say but even with  the game as violent as gta online the  vibes were just good  it reminded me of 2013 all over again  which was a big reason why i wanted to  make this video gta online next gen is a  fun place to be right now and i'm  hopeful that this feeling will last for  a while since the next gen console  market is such a joke but while people  are still waiting to bag a ps5 or a new  xbox more and more players will start  gta fresh just like us for years to come  okay here are some last minute tips for  anyone who is brand new to gta online  first remember to use your interaction  menu by pressing and holding the  touchpad on the ps5 or the view button  on xbox this sub menu's got a lot of  great shortcuts like enabling passive  mode which prevents people from killing  you if you need a moment it's also a  great way to eat some snacks and regain  health equip armor you've purchased and  even customize your character's moves  which you can do to anyone at any time  next is your phone your player's cell  phone is the hub of opportunity it's  where you go to find property listings  it's how you purchase a car and it's the  easiest way to deposit your money after  you complete a mission and get paid out  it doesn't directly go into your bank  account but rather your wallet which  people can pick off of your wasted body  so use the deposit feature and just use  your cell phone it's also the way to  interact with every npc you come across  your friends like lamar and lester all  have your back in one way or another hey  call me back when you found yourself a  brain  as you level up you'll get more  abilities like being able to put a  bounty on someone having a car delivered  to you wherever you need it and way more  if you're a veteran gta online player  feel free to leave more tips and tricks  of your own down in the comments  we hope you found this video helpful  show some love and drop a like if you  did and remember to subscribe to  gamespot for more videos just like this  thanks for watching  [Music]  you
 

